* 28 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux ec8459b - W.11 F10: the Xn, Dn and Ln records are sealed with a secret that only the new process is given (its environment); CPROC runs them
*               only if the seal checks.  $ipc is a file every SD user's process may write.
* 18 Oct 26 Windows port - from Linux 7f7a4fd (16 Oct 26): USER n: the phantom takes user number n, one of those the PHANTOMS parameter keeps (QM4 gaps).
